Provenance of torch_n3/blocks/denoise.py
========================================

`denoise.py` implements the non-local-means filter of

    Manjon, J. V., Coupe, P., Buades, A., Fonov, V., Collins, D. L., &
    Robles, M. (2010).  "Non-local MRI upsampling."
    Medical Image Analysis 14(6), 784-792.

Copyright (C) 2010 Jose V. Manjon and Pierrick Coupe.

The authors' own distribution of the method is Matlab plus a C MEX kernel,
`cMRegularizarNLM3D_V2.c`, which is stated by its accompanying header to be
GPL-licensed.  `denoise.py` is a PyTorch reimplementation of that kernel's
computation, carrying none of its code: it was written as whole-volume tensor
operations rather than as the original's per-voxel loop, and it differs from
the original by convention as well as by expression -- see the module
docstring, "Not the same filter as the C kernel".

It is nevertheless a derivative of a GPL-licensed work by descent, and it is
recorded here as such.  The remainder of `torch_n3` states no licence; the
sources it ports from carry the permissive MNI terms reproduced in
`torch_n3/_legacy/n3/COPYING` and `torch_n3/_legacy/ebtks/COPYING`.  Anyone
redistributing this package should settle the two against each other before
doing so.

The filter is off by default and is not part of N3.  Nothing on the default
path of `torch_n3` executes any of `denoise.py`.
